      "sequence_position": 7,
      "problem": "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $12≡36\\,(\\text{mod}\\,2)$\n- $-9≡18\\,(\\text{mod}\\,4)$\n- $21≡45\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we recall that \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,n∣(a-b).\n$$\n\nSo, $a$ and $b$ are congruent modulo $n$ if and only if $(a-b)$ is divisible by $n$ (there is no remainder).\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true because $2∣(12-36).$ There is no remainder:\n\n$$\n(12-36)÷2=-24÷2=-12\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false because $4∤(-9-18).$ Notice that $-9-18=-27,$ which is not divisible by $4.$\n\n- Statement III is true because $8\\,|\\,(21-45).$ There is no remainder:\n\n$$\n(21-45)÷8=-24÷8=-3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
